    "OtherAbstract": {
      "Type": "KIE",
      "Language": "eng",
      "AbstractText": "Eight prison inmates under death sentence in Texas and Oklahoma brought suit claiming that the use of certain drugs for execution by lethal injection without approval by the Food and Drug Administration violated the federal Food, Drug, and Cosmetic Act. In overturning a lower court ruling, the U.S. Court of Appeals held that the FDA had improperly refused to exercise its enforcement discretion to determine the safety and effectiveness of the drugs for lethal injection. As a result, the prisoners face the risk of execution involving torturous or lingering death, which is unconstitutional."
    }
